"entity": {
"name": "Enea SA",
"description": "ENEA SA engages in the production and transmission and sale of electricity to homes and businesses. It operates through the following segments: Retail Trade, Wholesale, Distribution, Conventional Energy Generation, Renewable Energy Generation, Heat Generation, Mining, and Other Activities. The Retail Trade segment deals with the purchase and sale of electricity. The Wholesale segment refers to optimization of the portfolio of wholesale energy contracts for electricity and gas fuel. The Distribution segment offers electricity distribution and transmission services. The Conventional Energy Generation segment is involved in the generation and sale of electricity and heat from conventional sources. The Renewable Energy Generation segment focuses on the generation and sale of electricity from renewable sources, such as water, wind, photovoltaics, and biogas. The Generation segment handles generation of electricity from conventional and renewable sources, as well as generation of industrial heat. The Mining segment includes production and sale of coal, and companies providing support services to mines. The Other Activities segment relates to maintenance and modernization of road lighting equipment, transport services, repair, and construction services. The company was founded on October 31, 1904 and is headquartered in Poznan, Poland. (Ultimate parent: Poland)",
